  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding a few atomic percent titanium to CoCrFeNi will promote in-situ formation of an oxide layer during sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sliding-induced oxide layer will be stable and lubricious.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer will protect the surface and maintain low friction and wear from room temperature through 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi matrix is single phase and contains no intentional secondary phases.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A few atomic percent titanium is the proposed alloy modification.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will produce a fine, uniform Ti-rich oxide layer at the sliding interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The interfacial layer may consist of TiO2 or mixed titanium oxides containing chromium or cobalt.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-rich oxide will act as a protective, low-shear film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Titanium has a strong tendency to form stable and adherent oxides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During elevated-temperature sliding, titanium oxidation will create a continuous lubricious oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide scale will reduce direct metal-to-metal contact and thereby reduce adhesive wear and friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, adding a few atomic percent titanium will minimally affect the primary microstructure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer will become more pronounced as temperature increases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-alloyed CoCrFeNi will have a significantly lower coefficient of friction than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout the room-temperature-to-800 °C range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-alloyed CoCrFeNi will have a significantly lower wear rate than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout the room-temperature-to-800 °C range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi tends to show increased friction at elevated temperatures because it lacks a stable protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "baseline",
